      "writtenOn": "2024-10-22T00:53:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done.\n\nI think this is slightly better because:\n\n* This avoids having to special-case `public_include_dirs` in `template(\"optional\")`\n* This ensures that only the GN/ninja C++ compiler and C++ stdlib are used.  In some scenarios Bazel may end up using a different, incompatible version of the C++ compiler and/or C++ stdlib.  It didn\u0027t matter so far for Fontations, but for Rust PNG it gave:\n\n```\n nm -C out/librust_png_cxx_bridge.a 2\u003e\u00261 | grep new_reader\n                 U rust_png$cxxbridge1$new_reader\n00000000000000b0 T rust_png::new_reader(std::__1::unique_ptr\u003crust_png::ReadTrait, std::__1::default_delete\u003crust_png::ReadTrait\u003e \u003e)\n$ autoninja -C out dm\n...\nFAILED: dm\nclang++ -rdynamic -Wl,-rpath,\\$ORIGIN -Wl,--start-group @./dm.rsp   -Wl,--end-group -lpthread -lfontconfig -lGLU -lGL -lX11 -ldl -lfreetype libfontations_ffi.a libbridge_rust_side.a librust_png_cxx_bridge.a librust_png_cxx_core_lib.a librust_png_ffi_rs.a -o ./dm\n/usr/bin/ld: obj/experimental/rust_png/impl/rust_png.SkPngRustCodec.o: in function `SkPngRustCodec::MakeFromStream(std::unique_ptr\u003cSkStream, std::default_delete\u003cSkStream\u003e \u003e, SkCodec::Result*)\u0027:\n/usr/local/google/home/lukasza/src/chromium3/src/third_party/skia/out/../experimental/rust_png/impl/SkPngRustCodec.cpp:238:(.text+0x9b): undefined reference to `rust_png::new_reader(std::unique_ptr\u003crust_png::ReadTrait, std::default_delete\u003crust_png::ReadTrait\u003e \u003e)\u0027\n...\n```",
      "parentUuid": "f556e88a_084b2848",
